<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 05:43:10 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East Live: US strikes Iran for first time in a month as Tehran retaliates against Jordan base</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month</link><description>
US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in their first military action in a month on Sunday, breaking a lull in fighting during an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. Iran swiftly vowed to retaliate for what it called a deadly attack. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/803bfff6-9ca4-11f1-a549-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T143107Z-71025016-RC2VXMAQM9SU-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-USA-CARRIER.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/803bfff6-9ca4-11f1-a549-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T143107Z-71025016-RC2VXMAQM9SU-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-USA-CARRIER.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6f7a1b4-a4c5-11f1-8a83-31d4a2f58c7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:02:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/803bfff6-9ca4-11f1-a549-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T143107Z-71025016-RC2VXMAQM9SU-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-USA-CARRIER.jpg">© US Navy via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz</link><description>
US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1532ba2-a4af-11f1-adf9-71be596dc8a3</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 20:27:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8e6966dc-a4af-11f1-a8ee-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4AZ2KD.jpg">© Atta Kenare, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank</link><description>
It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/27abccec-a44f-11f1-958b-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/israeli-settlers.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d4c4f894-a44b-11f1-9470-75564c8cf08f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 08:46:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu condemns 'criminal acts of violence' by settlers in West Bank villages</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday condemned what he called "criminal acts of violence" perpetrated by Israeli settlers in two Palestinian villages. Earlier in August, a group of settlers blocked supplies from entering Palestinian houses on the outskirts of Qusra and attacked a Palestinian family and a foreign media crew in nearby Jalud.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7144d52c-a3d4-11f1-873f-972eeb0bc107</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:34:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c2c9d0c8-a3d4-11f1-9dfa-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6TD3PD.jpg">© Jaafar Ashtiyeh, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran war reaches 6-month mark: Conflict cost $1,100 per US taxpayer</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer</link><description>
After six months of war, Iran’s leadership has coalesced around a hard core of military generals and clerics long entrenched in the ruling theocracy. They are ready for a potentially long confrontation with the US and determined to prevent any unrest at home. It’s a far cry from US President Donald Trump’s initial hopes of toppling the Islamic Republic and his subsequent claims that “regime change” had brought more compromising officials to the fore. In an analysis, FRANCE 24's Philip Turle said the war had so far cost around 1,100 US dollars for each US taxpayer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce883aa-a3bc-11f1-934a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170756-171246-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cce883aa-a3bc-11f1-934a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-170756-171246-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1e3089e-a3bc-11f1-b84b-775873edb3f6</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 15:24:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Situation in Niger 'not stabilised yet' as security forces deploy around airport</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport</link><description>
A group of soldiers in Niger rebelled against officers at a key military base and fired at sensitive locations in the capital, Niamey, in an apparent mutiny marked by gunfire and explosions, authorities said Saturday, in what was seen as a major threat to the country's struggling junta. FRANCE 24's Wassim Nasr brings you this analysis.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78eae0be-a3b1-11f1-b639-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-150807-151045-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/78eae0be-a3b1-11f1-b639-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-150807-151045-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7dd32f14-a3b1-11f1-9a04-c7d05d6e3460</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:59:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes on Gaza and West Bank</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank</link><description>
Israeli strikes in Gaza have killed five people, local hospital officials said Friday. Two brothers and another relative died in a strike on the family’s home outside Khan Younis, officials at Nasser Hospital said. Two separate Israeli strikes killed one person each in Gaza City, according to health officials at Shifa hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5690b0c-a394-11f1-9545-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120935-121116-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e5690b0c-a394-11f1-9545-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260829-120935-121116-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea5586ae-a394-11f1-8b90-d1c2be3b23b1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:34:58 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel army carries out rare West Bank air strike, killing 'three terrorists'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists</link><description>
Israel's military said it carried out an air strike in the Jenin area in the West Bank on Friday that killed a ​Palestinian it described as a Hamas militant operative as well as two of his accomplices, in a rare use of deadly Israeli air power in the occupied territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">45d4b240-a302-11f1-adc1-7d8ef64e4da5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:14:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fd7979b0-a2f5-11f1-9ae1-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-28T152358Z-1191338275-RC2R7NA7VEHT-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-JENIN-AIRSTRIKE.jpg">© Mohamad Torokman, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>There is no proof that this video shows a plane crash in Tel Aviv</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv</link><description>
A video showing an airplane rammed into the side of a building has been circulating widely on social media. While social media users are claiming that the video shows a plane that crashed in Tel Aviv after an Iranian attack, its origin remains unknown and its authenticity highly questionable. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3e76d02-a2df-11f1-905e-4f73667cf1bc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:31:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7b6c19b4-a2f0-11f1-a69a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/tel-aviv-2.jpg">© X</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA[Israel's 'retrospective incrimination: First we shoot, we kill & then find a reason why it happened']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened</link><description>
Liza Kaminov is pleased to welcome Nadav Weiman, Executive Director of Breaking the Silence. He says there is a troubling gap between how Israeli military operations in Gaza are publicly explained and what soldiers experience on the ground. Testimonies collected by Breaking the Silence suggest that this gap is not simply about individual incidents, but about the policies, assumptions and rules of engagement. The testimony surrounding the Nasser Hospital strike points to “retrospective incrimination”: rather than identifying a legitimate military target before an attack, evidence connecting those killed to Hamas may be sought afterward in order to justify the strike.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6fef0e6-a216-11f1-bf13-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-090754-091732-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e6fef0e6-a216-11f1-bf13-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260827-090754-091732-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec89d3a0-a216-11f1-babb-89eb5d329b51</guid><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:58:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Syria President appoints Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as presidential adviser</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-syria-president-appoints-kurdish-leader-mazloum-abdi-as-presidential-adviser</link><description>
Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa appointed Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as an adviser to the presidency, state media said on Friday. Abdi's appointment comes just days after he dissolved the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) as part of an integration agreement with Damascus.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87f26f28-a262-11f1-828d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/ecaf7fb26190f6f17a6e524791cd696b728c92b6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87f26f28-a262-11f1-828d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/ecaf7fb26190f6f17a6e524791cd696b728c92b6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8942303e-a262-11f1-b5d9-95e86b25df8d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:59:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/87f26f28-a262-11f1-828d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/ecaf7fb26190f6f17a6e524791cd696b728c92b6.jpg">© Bakr ALkasem, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran, Qatar hold Hormuz talks as US blockade squeezes Iran oil exports</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-iran-qatar-hold-hormuz-talks-as-us-blockade-chokes-iran-oil-imports</link><description>
Officials from Iran and Qatar met on Thursday in Tehran for diplomatic talks on the strategic Strait of Hormuz, as a US naval blockade chokes oil supplies to Iran amid a domestic shortfall. The meetings follow a week of intense diplomacy in Iran involving separate meetings with officials from Oman and Pakistani seeking ways to end the war and reopen Hormuz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0144a124-a20f-11f1-ac9a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/3a99f04c0e831574dc9a7047493ccbe23a273935.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0144a124-a20f-11f1-ac9a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/3a99f04c0e831574dc9a7047493ccbe23a273935.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01feecc8-a20f-11f1-aefb-e73b1e1b3ef1</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 12:01:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0144a124-a20f-11f1-ac9a-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/3a99f04c0e831574dc9a7047493ccbe23a273935.jpg">© US Navy/AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Driven by faith, Jewish activists stand up to settlers to protect West Bank Palestinians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-driven-by-faith-jewish-activists-stand-up-to-settlers-to-protect-west-bank-palestinians</link><description>
A group of Israelis who regularly travel to the West Bank to protect Palestinians who are victims of increasing attacks by settlers say their Jewish faith drove them towards activism. On Tuesday, at least five activists were injured while rushing to assist Palestinians being harassed by settlers in the village of Jannatah, near Bethlehem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/750869d8-a1fb-11f1-85af-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/90c731f3c368af901ae9ed678d921222b5f36eec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/750869d8-a1fb-11f1-85af-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/90c731f3c368af901ae9ed678d921222b5f36eec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">762c3448-a1fb-11f1-8927-196f834b7ce7</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:41:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/750869d8-a1fb-11f1-85af-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/90c731f3c368af901ae9ed678d921222b5f36eec.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Navigation, jurisdiction, costs: Iran, Oman attempt to hammer out Hormuz deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-navigation-jurisdiction-costs-iran-oman-attempt-to-hammer-out-hormuz-deal</link><description>
Iran and Oman are holding talks to try to reach an interim agreement for a controlled resumption of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz. The two countries have discussed a framework for a “temporary corridor” for shipping, according to a joint statement by the Iranian and Omani foreign ministries. But the plan faces several hurdles.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3748a8b2-a186-11f1-a403-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225375678305.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3748a8b2-a186-11f1-a403-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225375678305.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bfda9d8-a186-11f1-8d34-9b8655681d83</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:29:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3748a8b2-a186-11f1-a403-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225375678305.jpg">© Amirhosein Khorgooi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Syria: Why is the dissolution of the Kurdish forces significant?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-syria-why-is-the-dissolution-of-the-kurdish-forces-significant</link><description>
The Syrian Kurdish Forces announced their dissolution on August 25, in what is considered a significant step for Syria. FRANCE 24's Andrew Hilliar tells us why.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/340e837e-a168-11f1-908f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-SDF.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/340e837e-a168-11f1-908f-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-SDF.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7d246678-a168-11f1-8617-ebccca412597</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:16:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says he believes Iran’s leader is still alive but 'seriously wounded'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-middle-east-live-iran-says-hormuz-strait-still-closed-despite-transit-corridor-talks-with-oman</link><description>
President Donald Trump on Wednesday said he believes Iran’s Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei is “very seriously wounded”, but not dead. Khamenei has not been seen in public since the US and Israel launched the Iran war in February, prompting months of speculation over the new Iranian leader’s health. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b202c63a-82ca-11f1-8183-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195647347050.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b202c63a-82ca-11f1-8183-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195647347050.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">803a890c-a0d0-11f1-af96-4be69c450b59</guid><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 06:04:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b202c63a-82ca-11f1-8183-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26195647347050.jpg">© Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US-led Gaza peace board warns Hamas over kites after Israeli threat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-us-gaza-peace-board-hamas-kites-israeli-threat</link><description>
The US-led board overseeing the Gaza peace plan warned Hamas on Tuesday to halt militant activity, including flying kites, after Israel threatened retaliatory strikes. A Board of Peace official said Israel must also respect the ceasefire, limiting military action to responses to “genuine and imminent threats.”
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71071d0c-a0ca-11f1-bdf3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ES-20260825-121107-121253-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71071d0c-a0ca-11f1-bdf3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ES-20260825-121107-121253-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b6e116ea-a0cd-11f1-bd1f-4be69c450b59</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:49:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/71071d0c-a0ca-11f1-bdf3-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/ES-20260825-121107-121253-CS.jpg">© France 24</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Syrian Kurdish leader announces SDF dissolution after its integration into army</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-syrian-kurdish-leader-dissolves-force-that-spearheaded-jihadist-fight</link><description>
Mazloum Abdi, the commander-in-chief of the Syrian Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) on Tuesday announced the dissolution of the group in a televised speech from the presidential palace in Damascus. The dissolution followed the integration of SDF fighters into the Syrian military, said Abdi, and represented a major victory for Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fd5df24-9cd8-11f1-b755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1bcd16013745a91828d87da7a5826951d0aaf12a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fd5df24-9cd8-11f1-b755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1bcd16013745a91828d87da7a5826951d0aaf12a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8bbb268-a0b5-11f1-a8c6-899d66905d38</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 18:49:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4fd5df24-9cd8-11f1-b755-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/1bcd16013745a91828d87da7a5826951d0aaf12a.jpg">© Delil Souleiman, AFP (File)</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran offers $10 million to kill Trump's son</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-offers-10-million-to-kill-trump-s-son</link><description>
Iranian state media has aired a video that appears to threaten the life of Barron Trump, US President Donald Trump's youngest son. Since the start of the war in February, Iranian media have on multiple occasions circulated content threatening the president and family members.  The US Secret Service has confirmed it is aware of the video.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12058c46-a09b-11f1-a098-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minitrump.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/12058c46-a09b-11f1-a098-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/minitrump.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f04fe12-a09b-11f1-9a5e-8b65e2f76409</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:44:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US economic D-Day sanctions: 'Repeated bombing attacks across Iran failed to change the calculus'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-us-economic-d-day-sanctions-repeated-bombing-attacks-across-iran-failed-to-change-the-calculus</link><description><![CDATA[
Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Imran Bayoumi, Deputy Director & Resident Fellow at the Atlantic Council. He sees the Trump administration’s new sanctions strategy toward Iran as an attempt to seek economic leverage where military force has so far failed to produce any results. But its effectiveness rests on several unresolved assumptions. Chief among them is whether Washington can compel China, Iran’s largest oil customer, to comply despite Beijing’s growing economic resilience. Iran, meanwhile, has decades of experience curtailing sanctions and is again threatening regional escalation.
]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b421d0-a088-11f1-980e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260825-130316-130856-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88b421d0-a088-11f1-980e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260825-130316-130856-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f7dc05c-a088-11f1-9726-c92810ac702f</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:44:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>With sanctions and tariffs, US bets on its economic power to get what it wants</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/with-sanctions-and-tariffs-us-bets-on-its-economic-power-to-get-what-it-wants</link><description>
The US has announced a new wave of sanctions on Iran and has promised to sanction any countries trading with it - including China. It also comes as the US deepens a trade war with its neighbour Canada. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d7cb31a-9fc7-11f1-95d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2291195686.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3d7cb31a-9fc7-11f1-95d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2291195686.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">27effb72-a073-11f1-b870-f37e3236efe0</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:25:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US removes Syria off its list of state sponsors of terrorism</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-removes-syria-off-its-list-of-state-sponsors-of-terrorism</link><description>
Turkey has welcomed a US decision to remove Syria from its list of state sponsors of terrorism. The move rescinds a decades-old designation which came with severe economic consequences for Damascus. Corresponding sanctions relief for Syria have also been announced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d0187b4-a008-11f1-904a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-SIRIA-TRUMP-AL-SHARAA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1d0187b4-a008-11f1-904a-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/FOTO-PORTADA-EEUU-SIRIA-TRUMP-AL-SHARAA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95a3fffa-a083-11f1-ab3e-a529da291c81</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 13:18:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran threatens retaliation as new US sanctions hit already-struggling economy</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-threatens-retaliation-as-new-us-sanctions-hit-already-struggling-economy</link><description>
Iranian officials are maintaining their strong rhetoric against the US, after Washington announced a fresh raft of sanctions against Iran. Tehran has pledged to hit back with its own measures, while the country is already suffering from already high inflation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08ac3fe8-9ff4-11f1-80a7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236447179370.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08ac3fe8-9ff4-11f1-80a7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236447179370.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c28074be-a064-11f1-b118-b3f95dcbc72b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 09:36:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Trump says Strait of Hormuz demined, warns of ‘zero tolerance’ for new mines</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-mideast-live-oil-tanker-struck-by-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-off-oman</link><description>
President ​Donald Trump on Tuesday said all ​mines ‌within ⁠the ‌international waters of ⁠the Strait of Hormuz ​had been ‌removed or detonated, ‌and that ​Iran had been notified that any ship ​or ​boat ​placing new ​mines would be destroyed under a US “zero tolerance policy”. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2501d84c-a02b-11f1-9048-974cfc6ca322</guid><pubDate>Tue, 25 Aug 2026 03:31:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/42ba7fce-a094-11f1-8493-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236684484728.jpg">© Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's Netanyahu says Iran tried to assassinate one of his sons</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-israel-netanyahu-says-iran-tried-kill-son</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said on Monday that Iran had attempted to assassinate one of his two sons, without providing evidence or further details. “Iran tried to kill one of my sons,” Netanyahu told Israel’s Channel 14, as he discussed security arrangements ahead of the October 27 election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3e718304-a003-11f1-a342-5d06cd2e84ac</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:38:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b473bf6c-9d84-11f1-a6cf-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-10T111823Z-2133718736-RC2IULATYH0L-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA-PLAN.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Mohammed bin Salman in the City of Light: Does West value economic interests over 'Western values'?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/mbs-in-the-city-of-light-in-a-world-of-realpolitik-does-west-value-economic-interests-over-values</link><description>
Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Susanne Koelbl, Der Spiegel's award-winning foreign correspondent. According to Koelbl,, Emmanuel Macron’s decision to welcome Mohammed bin Salman at the Élysée reflects realpolitik in its purest form: 'Saudi Arabia had become too important for energy, regional security, investment and diplomacy in the Middle East to be permanently isolated. So Macron wanted to establish France as an independent, balanced power between the Mediterranean and the Gulf."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dff450b8-9f30-11f1-9709-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260823-201801-202643-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dff450b8-9f30-11f1-9709-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260823-201801-202643-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4e4576c-9f30-11f1-9c8e-ef311ee57a06</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:26:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>With 'rare' Paris talks, France hopes to cash in on Saudi investment programme</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/with-rare-paris-talks-france-hopes-to-cash-in-on-saudi-investment-programme</link><description>
Saudi's crown prince Mohammed bin Salman is in Paris to meet France's President Emmanuel Macron. The two leaders are to hold talks on a variety of topics, but first and foremost about the situation in the Middle East. For France, this is a chance to benefit from Saudi Arabia's Vision 2030 investment plan. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali is at the Elysée Palace and tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3bdca1e-9f9f-11f1-8a1c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/29e8bbc03d4ba08106c49a7160b576e2ed940108.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3bdca1e-9f9f-11f1-8a1c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/29e8bbc03d4ba08106c49a7160b576e2ed940108.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6063c9e-9fbf-11f1-a610-33955a5d7e40</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:52:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What could new US sanctions on Iran entail?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/what-could-new-us-sanctions-on-iran-entail</link><description>
The US says it is preparing to announce new sanctions on Iran. It's been billed an economic D-day and is expected to add further pressure on the country's economy that's already been battered from previous sanctions and a US naval blockade. The renewed economic pressure would not be the first time the US has used economic tools at its disposal to corner Iran. But what could the new measures likely entail?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac1a90c8-9fc0-11f1-8016-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236475592468.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ac1a90c8-9fc0-11f1-8016-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236475592468.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">98577fd6-9fbd-11f1-80b7-2bac959f9311</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:42:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>US unveils expanded sanctions aimed at Iran's 'economic asphyxiation'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-us-unveils-fresh-sanctions-to-sever-every-economic-lifeline-sustaining-iran</link><description>
The US on Monday announced an expansion of secondary sanctions it hopes will "sever every economic lifeline" ​that sustains ‌Iran, Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said at a press conference. The expanded sanctions target Iran's digital assets, technology, gold, aviation and shipping sectors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82ec75a0-9fbf-11f1-88c3-aff65ef5344c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 13:27:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/552900fe-9ff4-11f1-9dfb-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/348da3527c6d3d2c0b2149d797c9ea9560ee6767.jpg">© Kent Nishimura, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran predicts ‘another defeat’ for US after Washington's new sanctions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260824-middle-east-live-iran-warns-of-a-harsh-response-to-anticipated-us-sanctions</link><description>
Iranian Economy Minister Ali Madanizadeh on Monday warned of "another defeat" for the US after Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announced expanded sanctions against Tehran. Madanizadeh said Iran had a "two-year plan" to counter the new sanctions and dismissed Bessent's stated efforts to sever "every economic lifeline" sustaining Iran. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08ac3fe8-9ff4-11f1-80a7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236447179370.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08ac3fe8-9ff4-11f1-80a7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236447179370.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">11ba4d4c-9fa3-11f1-88bb-3bb782f253d8</guid><pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:50:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/08ac3fe8-9ff4-11f1-80a7-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26236447179370.jpg">© Vahid Salemi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
